1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,847
We know the players.

2
00:00:01,867 --> 00:00:04,182
Cart A and Cart B.

3
00:00:04,202 --> 00:00:06,049
Now name the strategies.

4
00:00:06,069 --> 00:00:09,784
Be aggressive does not tell a customer
which

5
00:00:09,804 --> 00:00:11,651
number is written there.

6
00:00:11,671 --> 00:00:12,585
High does.

7
00:00:12,605 --> 00:00:13,518
Low does.

8
00:00:13,538 --> 00:00:17,720
A strategy has to be something you can
actually

9
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:18,600
post.

10
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,139
Here is the idea.

11
00:00:20,159 --> 00:00:23,986
A strategy is what this morning already
allows you to

12
00:00:24,006 --> 00:00:24,864
post.

13
00:00:24,884 --> 00:00:27,172
No peeking at the other board.

14
00:00:27,192 --> 00:00:29,866
No third price at the last second.

15
00:00:29,886 --> 00:00:33,328
No speech to the queue instead of a
number.

16
00:00:33,348 --> 00:00:38,330
If it is not on the list, it is not a
strategy here.

17
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:41,179
Write the list before the customers
arrive.

18
00:00:41,199 --> 00:00:44,842
Keep only what this morning allows, and
cross out

19
00:00:44,862 --> 00:00:45,737
the slogans.

20
00:00:45,757 --> 00:00:49,400
For each cart that list is High or Low.

21
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,842
Nothing else is on the board.

22
00:00:51,862 --> 00:00:53,470
That gives four pairs.

23
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:57,847
Before you keep a phrase, ask whether it
is High or

24
00:00:57,867 --> 00:00:58,718
Low.

25
00:00:58,738 --> 00:01:01,901
If it is not, you changed the game.

26
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:04,289
Keep the list short on purpose.

27
00:01:04,309 --> 00:01:07,870
Next we name the payoffs on those four
pairs.

